From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchyvr <noreply@omarchyvr.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] nvkms, nvidia-drm: 2Heads1OR flip hang fixes

Fixes for flips that hang forever on merged (2Heads1OR) heads, as used by
the Pimax Dream Air at 7104x3840 with DSC.

1. nvkms-hw-flip.c LimitMergedHeadSyncObjects(): a 2Heads1OR flip programs
   the client's semaphores and completion notifier on the PRIMARY merged
   hardware head only; the secondary head's window follows through the
   interlock and flip lock that NVKMS already programs. The stock driver
   executes the same acquire/release/notifier on both window channels, so a
   late release from one head can overwrite the acquire value of the next
   flip: both windows then wait forever and the client's GPU queue waits for
   a release that never comes (vkQueueWaitIdle blocks, scanout continues, no
   Xid). Module parameter nvidia_modeset.merged_head_sync (0644, runtime):
   1 = primary only (default), 2 = acquire on both heads, release + notifier
   on the primary, 0 = stock behaviour.
2. nvkms-rm.c nvRMIdleBaseChannel() / nvkms-flip.c nvIdleLayerChannels():
   when a merged head's window cannot be idled, force-idle ALL merged
   windows together and ignore the interlock/flip lock between them. The
   stock code accelerated one window at a time, which cannot complete an
   update interlocked with the other window, so every modeset on the GPU
   failed (IdleAllSatelliteChannels) while such a flip was stuck.
3. nvidia-drm-drv.c: the revoke on file release (nv_drm_postclose) takes
   the modeset locks non-interruptibly. A SIGKILLed process releases its
   lease with the signal pending; the interruptible acquisition then failed
   with -EINTR and the revoke was skipped, leaving the connector granted to
   a dead file (every later vkAcquireDrmDisplayEXT failed until reboot). A
   grant held by a closed file is now also dropped at the next grant, and
   the revoke drops the grant even when the disable commit cannot be staged.
4. Diagnostics: when a layer channel cannot be idled, one "Stuck layer
   channel" line (pushbuffer GET/PUT, the last flip's semaphores) and, for
   merged heads, the last 16 flips. With nvidia_modeset.debug=1 the first 24
   flips after a merged head starts scanning out a surface are logged too.

GPUs: RTX 20/30/40 (Turing, Ampere, Ada). Does nothing on RTX 50
(Blackwell has no 2Heads1OR).
Headset: Pimax Dream Air.
Driver: 615.78.08.
Status: Ported by omarchyvr from 610.57.04, compile-checked, NOT tested on hardware.

From omarchyvr (laughtt, https://github.com/laughtt/omarchyvr,
patches/nvidia/nvidia-2h1or-flip-fix.patch; background:
analysis/nvidia-flip-hang.md there). License: MIT OR GPL-2.0, as
open-gpu-kernel-modules.
